## Shell Command Safety

Always use `execFileSync` with an argument array when invoking shell commands. Never use `exec` or `execSync` with a concatenated string.

```js
// correct
childProcess.execFileSync('git', ['rev-parse', '--abbrev-ref', 'HEAD']);

// forbidden
childProcess.execSync(`git ${userInput}`);
```

## CommonJS Only — No ESM Mixing

This project uses CommonJS (`require` / `module.exports`) exclusively. Do not introduce `import` / `export` syntax or mix module systems.

```js
// correct
const { something } = require('./something');
module.exports = MyClass;

// forbidden
import { something } from './something';
export default MyClass;
```

## Test Coverage for New Validation Rules

Any new validation method added to `BranchNameLint` must have a corresponding test in `tests/test.js`. Follow the existing sinon mock patterns used throughout that file.
